            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Around furance rough ilocated in basement wall



Around the basement door



Downstairs bathroom fan -  damper may have failed 



Pellet stove - supply air intake



Ducting rough in above dryer</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>There is lots of thermal bridging occuring in all of the walls. There is heat loss in areas of the walls where there is a junction such as the areas where the floor joist and walls are connected, and corners of the house. </mainWalls>
                <VentilationSystem>If you do any upgrades that insulate the home and improve the air tightness, you should consider having a proper ventilation system such as a HRV installed. This will help regulate proper air quality and will properly ventilate the home as well. </VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
